## The Seven Axioms

### A1. Topological Invariance (The Cryptologic Key Exists)

Every system $S$ possesses a unique, computable topological fingerprint:

$$K(S) = \bigl(\dim H^0,\; \lambda_1,\; \text{Hol}(\nabla),\; \beta_0,\; \beta_1,\; \ldots\bigr)$$

This key is invariant under superficial transformations (renaming, reformatting,
reordering) and changes only when the **structural topology** changes. It is the
system's DNA — its irreducible identity.

**Operational consequence:** Before any action, compute $K(S)$. After any action,
recompute $K(S)$. The delta is the action's true effect.

