### A4. Holonomy Detects Structural Lies (Path-Dependence = Inconsistency)

The holonomy of a connection around a cycle $\gamma$ measures whether traversing
the restriction maps returns to identity:

$$\text{Hol}(\gamma) = \mathcal{F}_{e_n \trianglelefteq v_0} \circ \cdots \circ \mathcal{F}_{e_1 \trianglelefteq v_1} \circ \mathcal{F}_{v_0 \trianglelefteq e_1}$$

If $\text{Hol}(\gamma) = I$: the cycle is **flat** — contracts are consistent.
If $\text{Hol}(\gamma) \neq I$: the cycle has **curvature** — there is a
structural lie (the system says different things depending on which path you
take to ask it).

**Operational consequence:** Non-trivial holonomy must be resolved before the
gate can pass. The `sheaf-explorer` agent flags these as "frustrated edges."
The `sheaf-architect` agent designs restriction maps that flatten the connection.

