### A5. The Spectral Gap Gates All Advancement (No Gap = No Ship)

The spectral gap $\lambda_1$ (smallest non-zero eigenvalue of $L_\mathcal{F}$)
determines the rate of convergence to coherence. It is the single most important
number in the system:

| $\lambda_1$ | Interpretation | Action |
|-------------|---------------|--------|
| $= 0$ | Degenerate — disconnected or fully incoherent | FAIL: do not proceed |
| $< 0.01$ | Weak — slow convergence, fragile coherence | WARN: iterate more |
| $0.01 - 0.1$ | Moderate — functional but improvable | PASS: may proceed |
| $> 0.1$ | Strong — rapid convergence, robust coherence | PASS: high confidence |

**Operational consequence:** The gate checks $\lambda_1 > \theta$ (configurable
threshold). If it fails, the dev-loop iterates. If it passes, the loop advances.
This is the V&V criterion. There is no override except explicit user force.

